Week 6 Research Update

This week, I reviewed my fourth research paper as part of my ongoing systematic literature review:

"The Role of Artificial Intelligence in Enhancing Business Analytics and Decision-Making: A Systematic Review."

Paper Reviewed

P004
Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI): Interpretation, Transparency, and Trustworthy AI.

Key Learning

The paper explains how Explainable Artificial Intelligence improves transparency, trust, and interpretability in machine learning systems.

Unlike previous papers that focused on Business Intelligence and Decision Support Systems, this paper emphasizes understanding *why* AI makes a prediction rather than only measuring predictive accuracy.

Some of the important concepts explored include:

- Explainable AI (XAI)
- Model Interpretability
- Transparency
- Trustworthy AI
- Human-Centered AI
- Responsible AI

Research Reflection

One important takeaway from this paper is that organizations should not only build intelligent AI systems but also ensure those systems remain understandable, transparent, and accountable for users.

This research continues to strengthen the theoretical foundation of my systematic literature review.

